---
/**
 * Panel de FAQs (nodo 200:876/200:872 en Figma, dentro de "Group 39"). Colapsado por
 * defecto (barra dorada clara "FAQs" + flecha) — al hacer click (ON_CLICK real de
 * Figma) se despliega un tablero de 20 preguntas en 5 filas x 4 columnas sobre un
 * fondo dorado más oscuro (--color-gold, no --color-gold-light), con separadores
 * verticales dorados entre columnas. Cada pregunta revela su respuesta (itálica,
 * blanca) al pasar el mouse (interacción ON_HOVER real de cada tarjeta, nodo 216:384).
 *
 * Las 20 preguntas son contenido real del cliente (ver CLAUDE.md), incluidas tarifas
 * reales. Se agrupan en filas de 4 para reproducir el tablero real; en mobile (donde
 * Figma no define un estado abierto explícito) se apilan en una sola columna dentro
 * de cada fila — decisión de responsive propia, documentada en CLAUDE.md.
 */
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How much does a private investigator cost?',
    a: 'Our standard investigative rate is $120 per hour. Surveillance assignments generally require a minimum of 4 hours per day for at least 3 days, depending on the case.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is there a minimum number of surveillance hours?',
    a: "Effective surveillance takes time. A subject's activities can vary from day to day, and multiple surveillance periods can help identify relevant patterns and obtain meaningful documentation.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How can I reduce the cost of my investigation?',
    a: 'Providing accurate information can help us work more efficiently. Photos, addresses, schedules, vehicle information, and known locations can reduce unnecessary research time and costs.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why should I be cautious of agencies offering very low prices?',
    a: 'A low hourly rate does not always reflect the total cost of an investigation. Ask about minimum hours, travel, equipment, reports, and additional fees before hiring an agency. Choose experience, professionalism, and transparency—not price alone.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why would an investigation require more than one investigator?',
    a: 'Multiple investigators may be necessary when a subject moves quickly, travels frequently, or when continuous surveillance is critical to the investigation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What factors can increase the cost of an investigation?',
    a: 'Costs may increase due to multiple investigators, extensive travel, complex surveillance, high-security locations, urgent assignments, weekend work, specialized equipment, or complex financial investigations.',
  },
  {
    q: "Can the subject's location affect the cost?",
    a: 'Yes. Investigations involving frequent travel between Miami-Dade, Broward, and Palm Beach County, or restricted and high-security locations, may require additional time and resources.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are travel expenses included?',
    a: 'Travel requirements are discussed during the planning process. Significant travel may involve additional expenses, which will be clearly addressed before services begin.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does it take to get results?',
    a: 'It depends on the case. Background checks usually take 24–72 hours. Surveillance investigations may take several days to several weeks, while complex fraud or financial cases may take weeks or longer. We provide realistic expectations based on your specific case.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much does an infidelity investigation cost?',
    a: "Most infidelity investigations range from approximately $1,500 to $5,000, depending on the subject's schedule, movements, and the amount of surveillance required.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you offer background checks?',
    a: 'Yes. Public Background Checks start at $39.99, while Comprehensive Background Investigations start at $250.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between a Public Background Check and a Comprehensive Background Investigation?',
    a: 'A Public Background Check provides a basic review of publicly available information. A Comprehensive Background Investigation involves more extensive research and analysis tailored to your specific needs.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you investigate someone if I have limited information?',
    a: 'Yes. However, the more accurate information you provide, the more efficiently we may be able to conduct the investigation and identify relevant leads.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are investigations confidential?',
    a: 'Yes. We understand that investigations can involve sensitive personal, legal, family, and business matters. Your privacy and discretion are always a priority.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you work with my attorney?',
    a: 'Yes. We provide investigative support to attorneys and law firms, including surveillance, background investigations, locate services, investigative research, and evidence documentation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you provide forensic accounting and financial investigative support?',
    a: 'Yes. TARGET INVESTIGATIONS coordinates specialized forensic accounting and financial investigative support through qualified professionals when required. Services may include fraud investigations, asset tracing, hidden asset analysis, business valuation, and litigation support.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much does forensic accounting cost?',
    a: 'Forensic accounting and financial investigative support starts at approximately $1,400. The final cost depends on the complexity and scope of the financial matter.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you guarantee results?',
    a: 'No ethical investigator can guarantee a specific outcome. What we can guarantee is a professional, discreet, and thorough approach to obtaining the facts. The Truth Is Our Target.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What information should I provide before starting an investigation?',
    a: "Helpful information includes the subject's full name, recent photos, address, phone number, vehicle information, social media profiles, and known schedules or locations. The more accurate information you provide, the more efficiently we can investigate.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I get started?',
    a: "Simply contact TARGET INVESTIGATIONS for a confidential consultation. Tell us about your situation, provide the information you have, and we will discuss the investigative options available. Don't live with questions. Get the facts. The Truth Is Our Target.",
  },
];

// Cada pregunta va numerada en Figma ("1. How much does…"); se agrupan en filas de 4.
const numbered = faqs.map((item, i) => ({ ...item, q: `${i + 1}. ${item.q}` }));
const rows = [];
for (let i = 0; i < numbered.length; i += 4) rows.push(numbered.slice(i, i + 4));
---

<details class="faq-panel">
  <summary class="faq-panel__summary">
    <div class="faq-panel__summary-inner">
      <span class="faq-panel__title">FAQs</span>
      <!-- Polygon 1 (200:866): "V" abierta — dos trazos navy de 6px con puntas y base
           redondeadas (path exportado tal cual de Figma, no un triángulo cerrado). -->
      <svg class="faq-panel__chevron" viewBox="0 0 34 27" aria-hidden="true">
        <path
          d="M3.017 3.017 13.516 21.201c1.548 2.682 5.419 2.682 6.968 0L30.982 3.017"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="6.034"
          stroke-linecap="round"
        ></path>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </summary>

  <div class="faq-panel__grid">
    <div class="faq-panel__grid-inner">
      {rows.map((row) => (
        <div class="faq-row">
          {row.map((item) => (
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button type="button" class="faq-item__question">
                {item.q}
              </button>
              <div class="faq-item__answer-wrap">
                <p class="faq-item__answer">{item.a}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

<style>
  .faq-panel {
    --u: 1px;
    container-type: inline-size;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .faq-panel__summary {
    display: flex;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    background: var(--color-gold-light);
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .faq-panel__summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-panel__summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-bg);
    outline-offset: -6px;
  }

  .faq-panel[open] .faq-panel__summary {
    background: var(--color-gold);
  }

  .faq-panel__summary-inner {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 68.125rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-panel__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .faq-panel__chevron {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 1.25rem;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--color-bg);
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
  }

  /* Abierto: la flecha rota exactamente 180° (rotación real de las dos variantes). */
  .faq-panel[open] .faq-panel__chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .faq-panel__grid {
    background: var(--color-gold);
  }

  .faq-panel__grid-inner {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 68.125rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.8125rem;
  }

  .faq-row {
    background: var(--color-bg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    padding-block: 0.875rem;
  }

  .faq-item:not(:first-child) {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(233, 195, 126, 0.3);
  }

  /* Pregunta: Inter SemiBold 13px/19.5px #E9C37E. */
  .faq-item__question {
    all: unset;
    display: block;
    cursor: pointer;
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: calc(var(--u) * 13);
    line-height: calc(var(--u) * 19.5);
    color: var(--color-gold-light);
  }

  .faq-item__question:focus-visible {
    outline: 1px solid var(--color-gold-light);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Respuesta: Inter Medium Italic 13px/19.5px blanca, 12px debajo de la pregunta;
     aparece en hover/focus (ON_HOVER → CHANGE_TO de cada tarjeta, p. ej. 216:351). */
  .faq-item__answer-wrap {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
    opacity: 0;
    transition:
      grid-template-rows 0.25s ease,
      opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .faq-item__answer-wrap > .faq-item__answer {
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: calc(var(--u) * 12);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: calc(var(--u) * 13);
    line-height: calc(var(--u) * 19.5);
    color: var(--color-white);
  }

  .faq-item:hover .faq-item__answer-wrap,
  .faq-item:focus-within .faq-item__answer-wrap {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* --- Desktop (≥1024px): medidas del componente Group 39 (200:870 cerrado /
       200:872 abierto) en unidades del frame de 1549px — escala por encima de ese
       ancho, como el resto de secciones. --- */
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .faq-panel {
      --u: max(1px, 100cqi / 1549);
    }

    /* Cerrado: barra de 117px, "FAQs" Fraunces SemiBold 44px/52.8px navy y triángulo
           en los extremos de una caja de 1081px. Abierto: el título baja a 34px del borde
           superior y las filas empiezan 57px debajo. */
    .faq-panel__summary-inner {
      max-width: min(calc(var(--u) * 1081), 100% - 3rem);
      padding: calc(var(--u) * 32) 0;
    }

    .faq-panel[open] .faq-panel__summary-inner {
      padding: calc(var(--u) * 34) 0 0;
    }

    .faq-panel__title {
      font-size: calc(var(--u) * 44);
      line-height: calc(var(--u) * 52.8);
    }

    /* Caja de render del vector en Figma: 34×26. */
    .faq-panel__chevron {
      width: calc(var(--u) * 34);
    }

    /* Tablero: filas de 1090px separadas 13px; 56px de aire al final. */
    .faq-panel__grid-inner {
      max-width: min(calc(var(--u) * 1090), 100% - 3rem);
      padding: calc(var(--u) * 57) 0 calc(var(--u) * 56);
      gap: calc(var(--u) * 13);
    }

    /* Cada fila (Frame 75…99): padding 24/50/3 (13 abajo en la primera), tarjetas de
           196px centradas con 30px + línea + 30px entre ellas. */
    .faq-row {
      flex-direction: row;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: calc(var(--u) * 24) calc(var(--u) * 50) calc(var(--u) * 3);
      gap: calc(var(--u) * 60);
    }

    .faq-row:first-child {
      padding-bottom: calc(var(--u) * 13);
    }

    .faq-item {
      flex: none;
      width: calc(var(--u) * 196);
      padding-block: 0;
      position: relative;
    }

    .faq-item:not(:first-child) {
      border-top: none;
    }

    /* Separador (Line 23…31): 1px #E9C37E, 53px de alto desde el borde superior. */
    .faq-item:not(:first-child)::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: calc(var(--u) * -30);
      width: 1px;
      height: calc(var(--u) * 53);
      background: var(--color-gold-light);
    }
  }
</style>
